en the race.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Gary Peters (D) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Michigan's open Senate seat features Democrat Abdul El-Sayed against Republican Mike Rogers after Gary Peters decided not to run again. Polls in the final two weeks of October consistently show El-Sayed ahead, with independent surveys reporting five-to-seven-point leads and Republican-sponsored polls showing a narrower race. Aggregated averages across several outlets cluster around a four-point Democratic edge.\n\nExpert ratings mostly place the race in Lean Democratic territory, with a few calling it a tossup, and prediction markets price Democratic odds near seventy percent. El-Sayed has raised far more money than Rogers, but outside groups have spent heavily against him, and public Democratic divisions, including a high-profile defection to Rogers, keep the outcome in doubt. The forecast expects El-Sayed to win by roughly four points, with enough uncertainty that a narrow Republican victory remains plausible.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.7769, "margin": 3.59}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.7646, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.7534, "margin": 3.2}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.7553, "margin": 3.4}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.6955, "margin": 3.2}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.7118, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.7565, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7778, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.755, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.7606, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.7617, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.7781, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.7877, "margin": 3.7}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.7047, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.7427, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.7248, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.7315, "margin"